## 2. Experimental section
## 2.1. Chemicals
All reagents with AR purity (analytical reagent grade) were purchased and used as received without further purification. Deionized water with a resistance larger than $18.2~\mathrm{M}\Omega$ was obtained from a Millipore Milli-Q ultrapure water purification system.
## 2.2. Catalyst preparation
The synthesis of $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66 was based on the procedure reported by Lillerud and coworkers with some modification [46]. Typcially, $\mathrm{ZrCl_{4}}$ $(0.24\ \mathrm{g},\ 1.029\ \mathrm{mmol})$ was dissolved in $60~\mathrm{mL}$ of $\mathrm{\DeltaN,N^{\prime}}$ -dimethylformamide (DMF) by sonication for $5\mathrm{min}$ . Then, the ligand 2-aminoterephthalic acid $(0.186\ \mathrm{g},\ 1.029\ \mathrm{mmol})$ and $0.15\mathrm{\mL}$ deionized water were added into the clear solution under vigorous stirring for $10\ \mathrm{min}$ at room temperature. Aftwards, the solution was transferred into a teflon-lined stainless steel autoclave. The tightly capped autoclave was kept in an oven at $120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under static conditions. After $24\mathrm{~h~}$ , the solutions were cooled to room temperature and the precipitates were isolated by centrifugation. The solids were washed with $40~\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF three times and followed by washing with $40~\mathrm{mL}$ of methanol three times. During each wash, the suspension was kept at room temperature for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ before being centrifuged. The solvent was decanted. Finally, the solids were dried at $150~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under vacuum. Pure UiO-66, was synthesized by the same method as aforementioned for the preparation of $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66 by using terephthalic acid as the organic ligand.
To prepare 2.0 wt. $\%$ Pd $.@\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66, $0.5\ \mathrm{g}$ of vacuum-dried $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66 was first dispersed in $30~\mathrm{\mL}$ of deionized water at room temperature, and treated with appropriate amount of hydrochloric acid to tune the $\mathrm{pH}$ of the slurry around 4. Then $1.68~\mathrm{mL}$ aqueous $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{PdCl}_{4}$ (0.0552
