## 4. Conclusions
In summary, we have developed an efficient heterogeneous catalyst consist of ultrasmall palladium nanoparticles immobilized on amine-functionalized metal−organic frameworks (2.0 wt.% $\mathrm{Pd}\ @\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66) by using a direct anionic exchange and subsequent gentle reduction approach. The presence of free amine moieties in the frameworks of $\mathrm{Pd}@\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66 is assumed to play a key role on the formation of uniform, well dispersed and leaching resistant palladium nanoparticles on the support. The prepared $\mathrm{Pd}\ @\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66 catalyst exhibits excellent catalytic properties in the hydrodeoxygenation of vanillin in aqueous media. The superior performance for $\mathrm{Pd}@\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -UiO-66 is due to the cooperation between the metallic Pd sites and the amine-functionalized MOFs. The research thus highlights new perspectives for amine-functionalized MOF material for biomass transformation.
